{"kind":"report","text":"Technical disposition only; no Source approval, activation, provider or deployment authority.\n\nThe explicit register11/root directory10/partition1/membership6/rules3/destination6 cohort is a sound reconciliation of the approved Draft4 against the current catalog. A new destination version is the appropriate boundary if partition-created applications retain automatic file publication: its accepted native creator proof differs from destination4/5. Neither substituting directory9 (which inherits directoryRules5, not file-aware8) nor widening applicationPublicationOrigin for every destination preserves both the file-aware factory and old admission meaning. Pin all siblings explicitly; preserve NEWEST, installed cohorts, caller defaults and old golden bytes. Do not imply that invitation-key cohort10/9/6 already includes file publication or D1.\n\nThe new policy needs a finite, exact proof chain, not directory-kind equivalence:\n1. The application's accepted native genesis: exact frame/incarnation/hash, digest definition, kind, ordinal, computed seed address and source FactRef; exact create message/request number and full creator ref.\n2. The exact partition entry which sent that create: checked entry/frame/hash, establish-application act, verified signed intent addressed to that same partition, matching definition/seed cause and sentBy proof for the exact message.\n3. That partition's accepted genesis under the explicit partition1 code object, its seed/address/full root creator, source FactRef and exact create-partition message/request number.\n4. The exact native root10 entry that sent it, plus the root's checked genesis/pin. Match generation/base, seed cause, message, partition address and accepted cohort; prove partition fixed root/membership/rules/destination values came from this root's actual native creation context. The destination's full immutable affiliation must equal that SAME root and the copied destination sibling, never a caller-supplied root-like scope.\nUse whatever bounded native defining/confirmation facts establish those fixed sibling refs; do not infer them from platform aliases or a mutable application field. This is one known root/partition hop, not recursive ancestor discovery or a history scan. State the fixed fact/read/byte/depth budget in Source. Missing/unavailable required evidence remains unresolved/dependency-unavailable; checked contradictory evidence is non-native. Do not manufacture a refusal entry, accept an incomplete chain, or fall back to old proof.\n\nRetain directoryRules8's activated-definition/closure checks, trusted opener, bounded canonical values and reserved destination handling in the new partition factory. The root creates/control-pins siblings once; partitions copy their full refs/incarnations. Membership6's native invitation behavior must come from explicit root creation/version tables, not merely exporting the cohort literal. Preserve original lane create/index body and routing semantics: a lane's immediate directory is its partition, while room-level authority/publication affiliation resolves explicitly to its proven root. A caller cannot choose those two meanings.\n\nImportant additional current-Source boundary: this is not only applicationPublicationOrigin. publishingLaneAffiliation and publishingLaneOrigin currently require seed.creator==destination's directory ref; nativeOrigin currently expects creator.under==platform:directory. Ordinary change/issue lanes born under partition1 will otherwise fail identity, reserve admission or the pre-send publication check, or be incorrectly admitted if these global helpers are widened by kind alone. Reconcile the reserved native-name proof, ordinary review-backed lane affiliation AND automatic application policy for the explicit new cohort. Keep destination4/5 accepted histories exact. Cover delivery.ts's new-request admission and operations.ts's publicationReady, the source/native origin producer in object/namespace, and replay with the same bounded checked chain. Do not treat a declared name change/issue or directory-kind partition as authenticated native identity.\n\nA per-version policy dispatch is needed at the actual consumer, selected by the receiving pinned destination/code owner, not by an untrusted request field. Adding a Platform catalog member alone is insufficient: runtime delivery/operations currently call imported global helpers directly. Replay currently accumulates one applicationPublicationOrigin callback and rejects different function identities when multiple supplied native versions disagree; account for mixed old/new histories with policy selection by the destination run's exact pinned version. Do not replace the old global callback in a way that reinterprets old journals or lets supply order choose admission.\n\nDestination6 inherits destination5's regular-publication standing journey and reviewed closure, including bounded exact signer/check provenance, all counted keys, \u003e9-key refusal, confirmed-mint/undecided-push discriminator, abort/revoke/deciding-read behavior, late cleanup and already-effective-send discovery. Automatic file publication remains outside D1's human-standing guarantee. Audit each closed destination4/5 branch at runtime/replay/host/receipt/site/checker/Page compatibility boundaries when adding6; reuse explicit closed supported versions, not \u003e=5/accept-all-future guards. In particular preserve the just-fixed fileSupersededOutcome behavior and lost-reply/unknown no-repeat behavior.\n\nQ6/Q7 still need the required Source search and real Authority witness: unrelated directory-kind senders cannot seal/relay/register or publish; the correct partition reads its fixed native membership (including membership6) before and after seal; root and partition consumers route distinctly even with their shared kind. Use real native factory creation through root-\u003epartition-\u003eapplication/change and destination6, plus wrong-root/partition/cohort/incarnation/seed/send/request/sibling/context and missing-proof controls. Synthetic alias/genesis fixtures alone do not establish the factory/Authority chain. Old4/5 controls must show no new accepted creator history; mixed-version replay must not select a new policy for an old run.\n\nPreserve Draft4's handoff, indexed bounded lookup, generation retries/unknown behavior, C1 reservations and C2 indexes. Real MAX_GENERATIONS1000 requires its full3000 standing root entries from genesis under the declared capacity; a smaller test-only maximum is a labelled control, not production capacity proof. No new scopeEntries constant/default rollout is authorized. This advice reconciles implementation boundaries; the eventual whole Source still needs exact-head review and its normal gate.\n\nBasis: approved Draft4 sections4/7/8/10/11(Q6/Q7), current application.ts/directoryRules8, invitation-key.ts/directoryRules9, register DIRECTORY_OF, directory SIBLINGS_OF, index version/default catalog, publishing-provenance.ts, delivery.ts, operations.ts and replay policy collection/application-origin construction. Read-only inspection; no Source change or test/provider execution.","body":{"formal_approval":"false","no_git_artifact":"true","promise":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e9e01703451b2ba69191ffb30d04b4e94c9d9da4","request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:91eec98584ac5866c14af65ee99355f19669e2b9"}}